WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:03.369
Welcome to NestWell.

2
00:00:03.919 --> 00:00:07.068
Gentle support for new mothers, and their practices.

3
00:00:08.600 --> 00:00:11.628
For a new mother, the twelve weeks after birth are full.

4
00:00:12.178 --> 00:00:14.660
Feeding, healing, and very little sleep.

5
00:00:15.210 --> 00:00:17.154
Follow-up care can quietly slip.

6
00:00:18.800 --> 00:00:20.186
NestWell has one aim.

7
00:00:20.736 --> 00:00:22.833
Help her complete the next step in her care.

8
00:00:23.383 --> 00:00:25.380
And let her practice confirm it happened.

9
00:00:27.100 --> 00:00:31.111
What you’ll see is a working demonstration, with made-up patients.

10
00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:36.939
On every screen, “I need help now” is one tap away.

11
00:00:37.489 --> 00:00:40.767
She also sees who to contact at her practice, and when.

12
00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:45.930
At set points, she answers a few short questions.

13
00:00:46.480 --> 00:00:49.945
She can skip a question, or leave the whole check-in for later.

14
00:00:50.495 --> 00:00:53.079
She sees no streaks, badges, or scores.

15
00:00:53.629 --> 00:00:55.436
Her answers are simply saved.

16
00:00:56.967 --> 00:01:00.922
If something feels urgent, she sees clear emergency steps,

17
00:01:00.922 --> 00:01:02.398
and can call from the screen.

18
00:01:02.948 --> 00:01:06.263
In a real practice, clinicians approve that wording,

19
00:01:06.263 --> 00:01:08.382
and it stays the same every time.

20
00:01:09.900 --> 00:01:13.275
Mood questions are optional, and not a diagnosis.

21
00:01:13.825 --> 00:01:17.572
She decides who sees her answers, and can change that any time.

22
00:01:18.122 --> 00:01:22.081
One safety question is the exception, and she is told up front.

23
00:01:23.800 --> 00:01:27.968
On the practice side, each request goes to a set role, with a clock.

24
00:01:28.518 --> 00:01:31.233
If no one picks it up in time, it escalates.

25
00:01:31.783 --> 00:01:34.385
And her phone tells her to call, not to wait.

26
00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:39.631
When her clinician makes a referral, the practice tracks each step.

27
00:01:40.181 --> 00:01:42.212
Sent, then scheduled, then kept.

28
00:01:42.762 --> 00:01:46.516
A referral counts when the appointment is kept, not when it is sent.

29
00:01:48.933 --> 00:01:53.163
After a pregnancy or baby loss, baby content stops at once.

30
00:01:53.713 --> 00:01:57.546
She chooses how she is addressed, and how often to be contacted.

31
00:01:58.096 --> 00:02:00.015
And nothing starts again on its own.

32
00:02:01.733 --> 00:02:04.683
AI explains clinician-approved material

33
00:02:04.683 --> 00:02:07.669
and drafts summaries for her clinician to review.

34
00:02:08.219 --> 00:02:13.532
It never triages, diagnoses, or reassures, and never takes a person’s place.

35
00:02:14.082 --> 00:02:16.763
The practice can also see where follow-up stalls.

36
00:02:18.367 --> 00:02:22.896
NestWell is in development, and looking for pilot practices in Ohio.

37
00:02:23.446 --> 00:02:26.418
To learn more, visit hellonestwell.com.
